{:org/id :org-fra-loi-1901-associations
 :org/name "Loi 1901 associations and equivalent association-law sectors (France, Japan 任意団体, US small 501(c)(3))"
 :org/entity-kind :org-form
 :org/form-family :family-association-law-sector
 :org/category :cat-local-place
 :org/type :secular-community
 :org/scope :global
 :org/region-primary :region-europe
 :org/countries ["FR" "JP" "US" "IT" "BE" "SN" "LU"]
 :org/founding-date 1901
 :org/instance-count-estimate 1500000
 :org/member-count-basis "llm-recall-unverified: France is commonly described as having well over a million active loi 1901 associations with tens of millions of memberships and roughly a fifth of adults volunteering in one; Japanese 任意団体 are unregistered by definition and uncounted."
 :org/legal-registration :registered
 :org/governance-model :democratic
 :org/mission-statement "The default legal shell a country offers to voluntary groups — the French 1901 law, the German e.V., the Japanese NPO法人 and 任意団体 distinction. What the shell requires (and how cheap it is) shapes how much of a nation's community life is visible at all."
 :org/related-org "org-deu-vereine"
 :org/coverage-note "Recorded because this corpus's central variable — whether a community is registered — is largely determined by what registration COSTS in a given jurisdiction, not by the community's own nature."
